    <h1>Melissa, TX's Best Plumbers for 2026: 4 Companies Compared</h1>
    <p class="rv-lead">Melissa's newest subdivisions — Liberty, Legacy Ranch, North Creek — are going up on the same Blackland Prairie clay that runs under the rest of Collin County, and a lot of that ground is still settling around fresh slab foundations. That's rough-in and slab-plumbing work, not just service calls, and it takes a crew that can pull a real permit and stand behind it. Our top pick for 2026 is <strong>Masters Touch Plumbing Solutions</strong>, the only one of the four physically based inside Melissa city limits and the only one carrying a Registered Master Plumber license (RMP #36569) we could confirm on record. The other three are all headquartered within a 20-minute drive — Little Elm/Frisco, Allen and Princeton — and each publishes a dedicated Melissa service page rather than a generic county-wide listing. We verified every name, address, phone number and license below against the company's own site plus at least one independent source before it made this list.</p>
